# Every committed WASM component in this repository, one per line.
#
# scripts/rebuild-components.sh reads this file. With no argument it rebuilds every line that is
# not frozen and copies the result over the committed output; with --check it writes nothing and
# names every non-frozen component whose murmur:* interface versions differ from the ones its WIT
# subtree declares. A test (crates/committed-components) runs the same check and also fails on a
# committed .wasm under crates/ that no line names, so adding a committed component means adding
# a line here.
#
# Columns, separated by whitespace:
#
#   name      what the command calls the component: `scripts/rebuild-components.sh <name>`
#   wit       the WIT directory its wit_bindgen::generate! names as `path:`; the check compares
#             the component against the `package murmur:*` declarations under it
#   source    the cargo package it is built from (a directory holding Cargo.toml)
#   features  cargo features to build it with, comma-separated
#   output    the committed .wasm the build is copied over
#
# Paths are relative to the repository root, and `-` means none. A line may end with
# `frozen: <reason>`, running to the end of the line: the command never builds or writes a frozen
# component, and the check reports it as skipped with the reason. A non-frozen line names a wit
# directory and a source; a frozen line may write `-` for either.
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.

